Carrier notes
raw_prime_count                        score=(1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0) :: counts primes but forgets residues, smoothing, and packet labels
mertens_mobius_cancellation            score=(1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0) :: keeps signed squarefree cancellation but not unit capacity
mu_over_n_explicit_tail                score=(1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0) :: normalizes Mobius cancellation by scale; useful tail guard
squarefree_unit_normalizer_G           score=(1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0) :: G(x)=sum mu^2/phi keeps inverse primitive-unit packet cost
selberg_quadratic_upper_packet         score=(1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0) :: quadratic upper-bound sieve declares lambda_d and kernel
large_sieve_minor_arc_packet           score=(1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0) :: large sieve controls families of phases/exceptions
circle_method_major_minor_split        score=(1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0) :: major/minor arcs retain local main term plus oscillatory error
explicit_formula_smoothing_packet      score=(1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 0) :: smoothing transform plus zero/exponential-sum terms are declared
kaczynski_boundary_approach_packet     score=(1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1, 1) :: exceptional/boundary approach class is retained as proof data
labelled_lrc_interval_packet           score=(2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2, 2) :: HYP-2981-style packet: endpoint, route, interval, and handoff labels

LRC14 theorem-facing readout
A Selberg/large-sieve packet is useful for LRC14 only as a middle certificate: it may bound a family of late denominators or exceptional phases, but HYP-2978/HYP-2981 still require endpoint, route, safe-measure, Fejer interval, Ramanujan, or state-lift labels.
New subtarget: prove a labelled analytic packet lemma for the HYP-2901 Node-3 wall: after small denominator packets are killed, G(z)-type inverse-unit normalization plus a declared smoothing transform forces a twist/Fejer witness or routes to HYP-2908.
